 "conventions": {
  "rig": "Mixamo skeleton from Sitting_Talking.fbx (65 bones), skeleton only, 30 fps, frames start at 1",
  "clip": "5.4 s: standing at the mark (0.27 s) -> 2.0 s accelerating run-up (v = 7.2 m/s (1 - e^(-t/0.75 s)), 6 steps, ~10 m) -> bound off the left foot (0.33-0.37 s flight) -> back-foot contact -> front-foot contact -> release at 2.93 s (frame 89) -> follow-through, 4 deceleration steps veering off the pitch, ends standing (field_clips STAND) facing the batter",
  "world": "the bowler runs toward the rig's forward direction (-y); his popping crease at y=0, his stumps at y=+1.22, the batter's stumps at y=-18.9; start_position_m gives the mark",
  "arms": "ra_ = right-arm over the wicket, la_ = left-arm over the wicket (mirror)",
  "ball": "attach the ball to the bowling hand (RightHand / LeftHand) until release_frame and launch it from release_point_m",
  "variations": "these are stock deliveries; the bowling_motions set's release variants (bouncer, yorker, cutters, slower balls...) and its delivery map still apply - use the release physics from that map with these actions",
  "biomechanics": "per clip, measured on the exported skeleton: knee angles are included angles (180 = straight); yaw 0 = chest square to the batter, -90 = side-on; separation = shoulders - pelvis; trunk angles of hips->neck from vertical (forward = toward the batter, lateral + = away from the bowling arm)"
